        <h2 class="text-center article-header">What to Expect During a Cosmetic Surgery Consultation</h2>
        
        <article class="article-container article-content">
          <p>Your consultation is the foundation of your journey with AURELIS. This comprehensive meeting ensures we understand your unique goals, discuss realistic outcomes, and determine if you're a suitable candidate for the procedures you're considering.</p>
          
          <h3>Why the Consultation Matters</h3>
          <p>The consultation is more than an initial assessment—it's the beginning of our collaborative partnership. During this meeting, we establish clear communication channels, discuss your aesthetic aspirations, and evaluate whether surgical enhancement aligns with your personal goals.</p>
          
          <h3>Discussing Your Goals</h3>
          <p>We create a safe space for you to express what you're hoping to achieve. Whether it's subtle refinement or more significant changes, we listen carefully to understand the underlying motivations and desired outcomes that matter most to you.</p>
          
          <h3>Medical History and Suitability</h3>
          <p>A thorough review of your medical history ensures your safety and helps us determine which procedures are appropriate for you. We discuss any health conditions, medications, or previous surgeries that may impact treatment planning.</p>
          
          <h3>Understanding Options and Limitations</h3>
          <p>Honesty is central to our practice. We provide detailed information about available options, their benefits, limitations, recovery expectations, and realistic outcomes based on your anatomy and goals.</p>
          
          <h3>Questions to Ask</h3>
          <p>We encourage you to prepare questions about the procedure itself, recovery timeline, potential risks, costs, and what to expect during healing. Your concerns are valid, and we're here to provide clear answers.</p>
          
          <h3>What Happens Next</h3>
          <p>If you feel comfortable moving forward, we'll discuss next steps including treatment planning, scheduling your procedure date, and preparing for surgery. If you need more time to consider, we're happy to schedule a follow-up consultation.</p>
          
          <div class="article-cta">
            <a href="#consultation" class="btn btn-primary">Book an Online Consultation</a>
          </div>
        </article>
